course: dictionary
lesson: 1491
title: Being careful
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Cautious means careful, so you try not to take risks or make mistakes. Think of a driver who looks both ways before crossing the road. «Rats are cautious with new food: they nibble a little and wait to see whether they feel ill.» The rat does not gobble everything. It tests a little first to keep itself safe.
explain: Cautious can also mean slow to decide or slow to trust. «Be cautious about strangers» means do not trust a new person straight away. It does not mean being rude. It means taking your time and checking first.
explain: In stories, cautious tells you a character is careful and maybe a little nervous. In maths and science, a cautious estimate is a careful guess that does not claim more than the evidence shows. Look for clue words around it, like danger, check or wait, to work out what it means.
fact: Cautious is an adjective, so it describes a noun: a cautious rat, a cautious driver.
fact: The comparative and superlative forms are more cautious and most cautious.
fact: «Cautious» means careful to avoid danger, risks or mistakes.
fact: «Cautious» can also mean slow to decide or slow to trust.
fact: In safety lessons, you should be cautious near roads, water, fire and online.
exercise: «Rats are cautious with new food.» What does cautious mean here? | *Careful, and testing a little before trusting | Very hungry and noisy | Greedy and quick to eat everything | Sleepy after a big meal
exercise: Which action shows someone is being cautious near water? | *Staying back from the edge and checking how deep it is | Running and jumping in without looking | Swimming out as far as you can | Splashing your friends
exercise: Mia says a cautious estimate is a wild guess. What is the best answer? | Yes, it means very big | No, it means fast | Yes, cautious means wild | *No, a cautious estimate is careful and does not claim more than the evidence shows
test: «Be cautious about strangers.» What does this mean? | Trust every new person at once | Ignore all people forever | Shout at new people | *Take your time and check before you trust
test: Ben's teacher says, «Your story shows a cautious hero.» What does cautious suggest about the hero? | Very tired and sleepy | Loud and bold | Funny and silly | *Careful, maybe a little nervous
exam: Which sentence shows someone being cautious? | The dog jumped on every stranger it met | *The girl looked both ways and waited before crossing the road | The boy ran across the busy road without looking | The man dived into the deep pool at once
